id: pm-rl-rsi
title: Promote improver policies from their own outcome ledger
description: "Add a typed versioned proposal policy, ledger-driven successor updates, equal-budget meta-task promotion, durable resume, and a three-generation CPU experiment over public tracker histories with two prediction targets."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T12:27:11.978Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T19:44:15.921Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[28]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T12:27:20.475Z",codex-agent,"Plan: retain the existing statistical promotion gate; add content-addressed finite search arms with Bayesian outcome priors, update candidates from development-only ledger outcomes, compare proposal policies on disjoint meta trackers under identical fit budgets, and open final audit trackers only after selection. Prediction features use strictly earlier history; chronological splits purge labels unavailable at their boundary. Record three generations, baselines, confidence bounds, actual kill/resume and behavioral revert proofs. Canonical sources remain read-only; dependency pins and thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T12:35:45.321Z",codex-agent,"Implemented two independent artifact levels: learner fits use the existing reserved process adapter and unchanged statistical gate; proposer artifacts contain bounded feature/optimizer arms with explicit outcome priors. Candidate priors are rebuilt from unique development-only proposal receipts. Meta challengers start from the same constant learner and receive identical candidate counts and optimizer updates. Confidence is allocated over planned comparisons; meta sample size is distinct trackers, averaging the related targets within each tracker. A frozen audit role remains unopened until all generations finish."
  "2026-10-19T12:46:00.699Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: retained all regression tests and replaced only the updateImprover prior-update block with return arm, preserving candidate version/ancestry/ledger metadata. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"improver updates actual\" test/improver.test.ts failed (exit 1: prior mass 16 instead of 116). Restoring the update passes; the combined update, leakage sentinel, chronological split and gate/feature regressions pass 4/4. The regression also asserts sampled proposals change, so a metadata-only update cannot pass. Real SDK/process tests additionally prove conditional inner promotion and gap rejection."
  "2026-10-19T12:51:22.942Z",codex-agent,"Leakage revert proof: replaced only historyBeforePrediction filtering with all events while retaining the sentinel regression. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"leakage sentinel\" test/improver.test.ts failed (exit 1); restoring the strict timestamp filter passes 1/1. A real SIGKILL after the first durable update resumes three generations, adopts original settled reservations, and replays terminal state without new jobs. The audit compartment is absent until all three selection receipts commit. The complete synthetic acceptance passed 8/8; final coverage and release gates are being run. Runtime diagnostics motivate a fixed four-tracker, K=1 live cohort selected solely from the existing manifest ordering/roles; statistical underpower is an explicit limitation, not a claimed gain."
  "2026-10-19T13:06:20.257Z",codex-agent,"Release diagnostics corrected scratch hygiene: the source copier now checks out only .agents/pm, with a committed-code exclusion sentinel, while retaining verified Git objects and public commit pins. Canonical checkouts remain unchanged. Strict lint passes after replacing mutable cross-await learner/policy locals with append-only incumbent arrays; this preserves phase inputs and numerical behavior. Duplicate count is zero; all 316 declarations across 44 authored files are documented. The complete isolated npm release gate is running at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-19T13:16:31.695Z",codex-agent,"Completed real public-tracker acceptance: three generations, K=1, 34 reserved CPU fits and 8704 fixed SGD updates in 878412.013029 ms (below 20 minutes), zero model tokens. Every development, meta and final audit retained score is 0.50 on the balanced time-to-close and Issue/other targets, matching majority and the retained constant seed. The outer sample unit is two independent meta trackers (100 target examples), below minSamples=10; all three improvers refuse with insufficient_samples, gain 0 and lower bound -2.701813717997259. Candidate failure priors change after 2/4/6 unique development outcomes; the incumbent artifact remains version 1. The final-code repetition and full release gates are running. The report makes no real-data improvement claim; pm-rl-rsipower tracks the required powered follow-up."
  "2026-10-19T13:51:52.848Z",codex-agent,"Added bounded in-flight recovery: every logical fit has at most two predeclared process slots, each launched at most once. A SIGKILL after a persisted launch intent with a missing or partially written completion can consume the second slot with identical training data and source parameters; the first failed reservation and conservative charge remain audited. Complete invalid receipts refuse, cancellation does not retry, and exhausting both attempts cannot allocate a third. The real SDK/OS test passes 1/1 across missing, partial, invalid, cancellation, trainer-failure and storage-fault scenarios. Normal 34-fit runs still perform 8704 SGD updates; recovery capacity is capped at 68 process jobs and 17408 updates within the unchanged whole-run deadline. Both meta contenders receive that same cap."
  "2026-10-19T13:59:40.012Z",codex-agent,"Final regression review also preserves learned priors when a promoted improver starts a later programme: updateImprover accepts a declared baseline, and the controller rebuilds its cumulative ledger from its immutable initial artifact. Tests prove incremental updates retain prior evidence and explicit cumulative updates count it once. Promoted ledger outcomes with nonpositive gain now refuse. All four pure policy/leakage/time/gate checks pass. The model, data splits, seeds and gate thresholds are fixed; remaining changes concern artifact accounting and bounded crash recovery."
  "2026-10-19T14:16:23.689Z",codex-agent,"Final measured source acceptance: 568392.653785 ms (9m28s), 34 successful reserved jobs, 8704 nominal SGD updates, no recovery use, zero tokens. Fixed recovery capacity is 68 jobs/17408 updates; all nine recorded numerical implementation hashes match the final source. Meta gain remains zero in each of three generations; both task baselines and audit scores remain 0.50. Fresh isolated behavioral copies independently fail with only prior updates reverted (exit 1), only recovery reverted (exit 1), or only the strict timestamp filter reverted (exit 1); restored pure regressions pass 4/4 and restored pre-exec SIGKILL recovery passes 1/1. The local complete release attempt hit the existing packed-LM 20-second smoke at 58.5 seconds under shared host load. No bound or threshold was changed; the complete npm/Bun matrix will provide final source-head verification. Existing timing follow-up pm-rl-7c7m remains separate."
  "2026-10-19T14:24:57.127Z",codex-agent,"Fresh committed-head clone passes strict tracker health with required merge drivers (exit 0) in an isolated HOME. The working host has an optional global pm-github host-version skew, distinct from tracked-project health; no pin bump or history repair is needed. Fresh-checkout test review adds creation of the ignored acceptance directory before taking its baseline inventory, so the real packed-worker test does not depend on prior local runs. PR 88 is open as a draft while the complete source-verification matrix runs."
  "2026-10-19T14:42:37.565Z",codex-agent,"Required complete gates passed on source head 117b7fdcb68b3d8b3eba2272b5d95eb88ea8e7ee in CI run 39268778334: npm run release:check (Node 26), 650/650 tests, 0 failures, 44 source files present, statements/lines/branches/functions all 100.00%; bun run release:check (Node 26), 650/650 tests, 0 failures, the same 44-file four-metric 100.00% coverage. Both isolated-identity gates also passed typecheck, build, strict lint, zero duplicate clones, all 320 declarations documented, publish-attestation verification, identity audit, zero production vulnerabilities, package dry-run and changelog check. CI tracker health passed with required merge drivers; CodeQL passed. Receipts: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39268778334 . The separate Node 22 compatibility job remains running. No dependencies, statistical gates, runtime smoke limits, coverage thresholds or history records were rewritten. Working-host optional-extension version skew and the locally failed packed-LM timing check remain separate from successful clean CI evidence. Explicit --author is required for injected extension-client attribution because PM_AUTHOR alone is not forwarded. PR 88 remains unmerged; final receipt-head verification follows."
  "2026-10-19T14:45:06.633Z",codex-agent,"Verification correction: run 39268778334 tested GitHub PR merge tree 9d7a05f09892e2d93158b8355ba910581d927bc0, combining implementation head 117b7fd with main 6715098. Main received the Dependabot toolchain update during this task. Reclaiming briefly to merge that already-approved main update into the branch, preserving append-only history, so the final branch dependency graph matches the complete gate evidence. The measured numerical source hashes remain unchanged. No hand-authored dependency bump is being introduced."
  "2026-10-19T14:46:48.580Z",codex-agent,"Main synchronized by merge commit 486ea9a137ac63cdebb61a1bc46b062c071ce294; only the existing Dependabot toolchain pins and built-in Git merge-driver test adjustment were inherited. No PM merge receipts were produced and no history reconciliation or rewriting was performed. The completed prior integration matrix passes all three jobs: npm Node 22, npm Node 26 and Bun Node 26, each 650/650 tests with 44 source files and 100.00% statements, lines, branches and functions. Local final improver component acceptance separately passes 9/9 tests with all five added implementation modules at 100.00% native line/branch/function coverage. Required four-metric evidence is the full matrix. Final branch content now includes the same main toolchain; a complete final-head matrix and fresh-clone health check follow. Measured numerical sources and the 568.393-second real-data null are unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T15:52:39.726Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: verified all four unresolved review findings against c8c8713 and read both review bodies; no additional outside-diff finding is present. Fix exact repository identity matching, finite numeric learning rates, post-install deadline accounting and finally-based live fixture cleanup. Add held-out candidate class counts, distinct predictions and train-versus-majority diagnostics with behavioral revert proofs. Because measured source changes, repeat the fixed real-data programme once; keep unchanged promotion, timeout and coverage thresholds."
  "2026-10-19T15:56:34.200Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 restored focused acceptance passes 5/5: cleanup, finite learning rate, exact repository binding, real candidate diagnostics and packed worker deadline/refusal. Behavioral revert proofs retain tests: removing Number.isFinite fails learning-rate rejection; restoring suffix lookup fails repository binding; removing fixture finally removal fails the before/after directory assertion; moving timeout calculation before pack/install fails the package-exists timing assertion. Each revert exits 1, and the implementation is restored. Linked pm test execution passes both commands (4/4 original pure cases plus 2/2 new pure cases). Strict lint, zero duplicate clones and docstrings pass. Starting the one allowed measured repetition with fixed pins, seed, fit/update budget and unchanged statistical gates."
  "2026-10-19T15:59:55.953Z",codex-agent,"The first two complete measured generations disprove uniform collapse: generation 1 has 0/10 constant candidates and 10/10 beat training majority; generation 2 has 4/10 constant candidates and 6/10 beat training majority. All retained learners remain at 0.50 because inner gates refuse candidates; the outer gate also remains below its minimum tracker count. Final counts and the README interpretation will use the completed run, including untouched final audit diagnostics. All three linked PM test commands pass (4/4 plus 2/2 plus 1/1); the repository-binding command succeeds through the current pinned runner."
  "2026-10-19T16:02:08.395Z",codex-agent,"Completed the single measured repetition in 244523.358157 ms with the identical sealed dataset, seed 42, 34 successful jobs, 8704 SGD updates, zero recovery jobs and zero tokens. All nine recorded implementation hashes match current source. Across development and both meta searches, generation constant-held-out counts are 0/10, 4/10, 5/10; train-majority winners are 10/10, 6/10, 7/10. Thus 21/30 candidates predict both held-out classes and 23/30 beat training majority. Candidate held-out accuracy ranges 0.375 to 0.666667. Audit has 2/4 constant and 2/4 training-majority winners, with candidate accuracies 0.375/0.50. No learner or proposer is promoted; retained scores remain 0.50 and two meta trackers remain below ten. README and docs distinguish constant-seed gate retention plus outer underpower from universal collapse. Full per-candidate aggregate diagnostics and refreshed resource/timing receipts are in docs/improver-live-evidence.json."
  "2026-10-19T16:03:24.549Z",codex-agent,"The source-hash check succeeded through Node -e: all nine recorded implementation hashes match current source. A distinct existing import issue was reproduced with a valid Node stdin entrypoint, deduplicated against stdin and launcher items, and recorded as pm-rl-stdin without changing the launcher. The remaining complete release matrix is pending; thresholds, dependency pins and gate limits remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T16:21:27.464Z",codex-agent,Pushed round-1 implementation and measured diagnostics as 3d4fb1019ca4bbb05e654ff36e5d21e7bebdd16f. A fresh no-local clone of that head passes strict tracker health with required merge drivers. Complete isolated-identity npm and Bun release gates are progressing without failures so far; GitHub CI remains queued. Added a precise constant-seed class-count assertion for the final verification commit. Existing history is independently verified byte-for-byte append-only. Threads remain untouched and the PR remains unmerged.
  "2026-10-19T16:23:15.875Z",codex-agent,"External CI delay confirmed: GitHub reports an active Actions/Pages/Webhooks incident with delayed workflow processing, starting before this task push. CI run 39282564621 remains queued with no jobs executed. Incident: https://www.githubstatus.com/incidents/8tzbpcnl75jp . Both local isolated-identity release gates continue without failures so far. Do not interpret queued jobs as passing checks or change repository CI to bypass this provider incident."
  "2026-10-19T16:29:34.341Z",codex-agent,"The local npm release attempt hit the existing packed-LM smoke timing assertion: 26719.014172 ms against its unchanged 20000 ms bound. All improver component checks passed before that unrelated failure. The failed npm process group was stopped to remove contention while Bun finishes; it is not counted as passing evidence. The existing timing follow-up is pm-rl-7c7m. No bound, dependency or threshold is changed. A complete sequential npm retry will use the already-installed Node 26 runtime matching CI."
  "2026-10-19T16:33:39.774Z",codex-agent,"Complete CI run 39282564621 is successful for source head 3d4fb1019ca4bbb05e654ff36e5d21e7bebdd16f: npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26, and bun run release:check on Node 26 each report 653/653 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, 44/44 measured source files and 100.00% statements, lines, branches and functions. Full logs include successful changelog checks and job completion; all remaining release checks and Bun package graph installs complete. CI checkout 8e73d46b9408b3bb9e07bc8824f4ad5e8677fbb3 and source head have identical tree dabe25129cfc8d36dc35a2d101f8a65862ca03ec. Receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39282564621 . GitHub incident delays individual check status delivery despite completed logs and successful aggregate conclusion. The redundant local Bun attempt was stopped after its improver checks, including the stricter constant-class assertion, passed; neither canceled local attempt is counted as a successful gate. Final verification commit adds that assertion and these receipts; numerical source hashes remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T16:34:44.254Z",codex-agent,"Additional strict class-key verification passes on Node 26: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"reserved fits\" test/improver.test.ts reports 1/1 with zero failures, including constant seed held-out classes exactly zero class-zero and all class-one. All nine measured implementation hashes still match current source. The final receipt commit changes only this regression assertion, documentation and append-only PM evidence; no learner, data, controller, statistical or resource code changes."
  "2026-10-19T18:20:33.164Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 at 345f3d4: confirmed legacy receipts omit candidate diagnostics but share the current binding. Add a receipt schema marker to the immutable digest and regress interrupted resume and completed replay using real temporary ledgers, requiring typed loop_step_drift before any new fit. Preserve current-schema resume. Latest review body contains one inline finding and no outside-diff findings. Run behavior-only revert proof and unchanged npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-19T18:22:49.533Z",codex-agent,"Regression passes 1/1 with real temporary SDK ledger and five actual process fits: a diagnostics-free interrupted ledger refuses at programme with loop_step_drift and zero new jobs; restoring current receipts resumes exactly four remaining fits; diagnostics-free completed replay also refuses before any phase or new job. Behavior-only revert removes only the receipt marker: unchanged regression exits 1 with TypeError reading beats_train_majority after adopting old receipts. Restored marker. Typecheck, test compilation, lint and zero-duplicate checks pass. Linked regression uses snapshot workspace and no PM context to avoid the existing tracker-spawning sandbox issue."
  "2026-10-19T18:23:30.070Z",codex-agent,"Linked PM verification passed all four commands: 4/4, 2/2, 1/1 and the new schema regression 1/1 (eight tests total), zero failures. Snapshot workspace with pm_context_mode=none runs the real temporary-tracker regression successfully without the existing sandbox collision. Running release gates sequentially on installed Node 26 with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config."
  "2026-10-19T18:55:39.408Z",codex-agent,"npm run release:check passed on Node 26 with isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1: 654/654 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, all 44 authored source files reported, statements/lines/branches/functions each 100.00%. Typecheck, build, lint, zero duplicates, docstrings, publish-attestation verification, identity audit, production audit, pack dry run and changelog check all passed. New legacy-ledger regression also passed in the full coverage run. The unchanged packed LM 20-second bound passed with measured CLI time 9953.044 ms. Starting the separate Bun release gate sequentially."
  "2026-10-19T19:44:15.920Z",codex-agent,"Local Bun release attempt is failed evidence: 653/654 tests, one ENOENT reading partial.json in the unrelated wall-expiry/AbortSignal test at test/process.test.ts:79. New schema regression passes within that run; reported line/branch/function coverage remains 100 percent. The unchanged failing fixture passes alone 1/1 with isolated identity. Native-fixture follow-up pm-rl-processcancel records this separately from Compose task pm-rl-8nev. No unrelated test or deadline was changed. Re-read latest review 5575756668: no outside-diff findings. Push the schema fix with this receipt and verify the complete unchanged npm/Bun CI matrix before final handoff."
